config EXAMPLES_XLAT
	bool "xlat: cross-domain latency probe (Jailhouse IVSHMEM)"
	default n
	---help---
		Periodic timestamp probe running inside a NuttX Jailhouse inmate.

		It measures the in-cell wake-up jitter (t_wake - t_deadline) and
		publishes each sample's timestamps to the IVSHMEM rw_section so
		that the root cell Linux can measure the cross-domain delivery
		latency and its jitter.

		The app never prints to the console: the NuttX serial driver is
		interrupt driven and blocking, so any printf inside the measurement
		loop would perturb the measured object.

		Requires the cell config to declare the IVSHMEM regions
		(see crtos/jailhouse_overlay_pi4/configs/arm64/rpi4-nuttx.c).
